= EFI Boot Process

:toc: left
:icons: font
:sectlinks:

See also: link:index.html[Main Boot Page], link:bios-boot.html[BIOS Boot Process], link:../roadmap.html[Roadmap]

NOTE: The EFI boot path is a *planned design* only. Source stubs exist at
`boot/efi/x86_64/` and `boot/efi/aarch64/`, but no EFI bootloader is
functional yet. i686 has no EFI target.

[cols="1,1,4,3",options="header"]
|===
|Phase |Component |Description |Mechanism / UEFI Protocol

|Preparation
|GPT partitioning
|The disk must use a GUID Partition Table. The bootloader lives in the EFI System Partition (ESP).
|Hardware standard (GPT); FAT32 filesystem.

|Entry
|EFI main
|The entry point of the loader receives a handle to the loaded image and a pointer to the system table.
|`EFI_STATUS efi_main(EFI_HANDLE image, EFI_SYSTEM_TABLE *sys)`

|System info
|Memory map
|UEFI maintains a more detailed memory map than BIOS. The bootloader retrieves it and later calls ExitBootServices to take ownership.
|`GetMemoryMap()` via Boot Services.

|Graphics
|GOP (Graphics Output)
|UEFI has no VGA. The bootloader requests a pointer to the linear framebuffer to draw pixels.
|EFI_GRAPHICS_OUTPUT_PROTOCOL

|File access
|Simple file system
|The firmware already provides a FAT32 driver, so the bootloader only needs to open the kernel file.
|EFI_SIMPLE_FILE_SYSTEM_PROTOCOL

|Kernel prep
|Memory allocation
|The loader allocates specific memory pages for the kernel segments.
|`AllocatePages()` with `AllocateAddress`.

|Handoff
|Exit boot services
|*CRITICAL:* shuts down the firmware drivers and gives the kernel full control of the CPU.
|`ExitBootServices()`

|Transition
|Virtual mapping
|Optional but common: UEFI runs in identity-mapped long mode; the loader may set up its own page tables here.
|MOV CR3, <table_address>

|Handoff
|Final jump
|UEFI already runs in 64-bit (or 32-bit) mode, so the loader can call the kernel entry point directly.
|`((void (*)(BOOT_Info *))kernel_entry)(s_bootInfo);`
|===

== Current Implementation Status

The EFI bootloader is not yet implemented. Source stubs exist at `boot/efi/x86_64/` and `boot/efi/aarch64/` (license headers only); there is no `boot/efi/i686/` target. The table above describes the intended design.

